# Paths exempt from LAYER 3 ONLY — the "does this look like a credential" scan.
#
# Layers 1 and 2 are NOT affected and cannot be opted out of: you can never
# commit .env, and you can never commit a real value from it. That is deliberate.
# A bypass that reaches the layer which catches actual secrets is not a bypass,
# it is a hole.
#
# One git pathspec per line.

# A secret-scanner's own tests must contain credential-shaped strings — that is
# what they are for. Without this the package can never test its own patterns.
packages/secret-scan/test/*
